null,"mana_cost":"{3}{W}{W}","name":"Serra Angel","oracle_id":"4b7ac066-e5c7-43e6-9e7e-2739b24a905d","oracle_text":"Flying\nVigilance (Attacking doesn't cause this creature to tap.)","power":"4","produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2026-04-24","toughness":"4","type_line":"Creature — Angel"},{"cmc":1.0,"color_identity":[],"colors":[],"defense":null,"keywords":[],"layout":"normal","legalities":{"alchemy":"not_legal","brawl":"not_legal","commander":"legal","competitivebrawl":"not_legal","duel":"banned","future":"not_legal","gladiator":"not_legal","historic":"not_legal","legacy":"banned","modern":"not_legal","oathbreaker":"banned","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"not_legal","paupercommander":"not_legal","penny":"not_legal","pioneer":"not_legal","predh":"legal","premodern":"not_legal","standard":"not_legal","standardbrawl":"not_legal","timeless":"not_legal","tlr":"banned","vintage":"restricted"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{1}","name":"Sol Ring","oracle_id":"6ad8011d-3471-4369-9d68-b264cc027487","oracle_text":"{T}: Add {C}{C}.","power":null,"produced_mana":["C"],"released_at":"2026-06-26","toughness":null,"type_line":"Artifact"},{"cmc":5.0,"color_identity":["G"],"colors":["G"],"defense":null,"keywords":[],"layout":"normal","legalities":{"alchemy":"not_legal","brawl":"not_legal","commander":"legal","competitivebrawl":"not_legal","duel":"legal","future":"not_legal","gladiator":"not_legal","historic":"not_legal","legacy":"legal","modern":"legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"legal","paupercommander":"legal","penny":"legal","pioneer":"not_legal","predh":"legal","premodern":"legal","standard":"not_legal","standardbrawl":"not_legal","timeless":"not_legal","tlr":"not_legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{4}{G}","name":"Spined Wurm","oracle_id":"05425f2f-7228-4bf5-8fe1-6fe99107e8e0","oracle_text":"","power":"5","produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2015-05-06","toughness":"4","type_line":"Creature — Wurm"}],"fixture_kind":"public_exact-list_card_data","rulings":[{"comment":"An effect that checks whether you control your commander is satisfied if you control one or both of your two commanders.","oracle_id":"584cee10-f18c-4633-95cc-f2e7a11841ac","published_at":"2020-11-10","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Both commanders start in the command zone, and the remaining 98 cards (or 58 cards in a Commander Draft game) of your deck are shuffled to become your library.","oracle_id":"584cee10-f18c-4633-95cc-f2e7a11841ac","published_at":"2020-11-10","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If something refers to your commander while you have two commanders, it refers to one of them of your choice. If you are instructed to perform an action on your commander (e.g. put it from the command zone into your hand due to Command Beacon), you choose one of your commanders at the time the effect happens.","oracle_id":"584cee10-f18c-4633-95cc-f2e7a11841ac","published_at":"2020-11-10","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If your Commander deck has two commanders, you can only include cards whose own color identities are also found in your commanders' combined color identities. If Falthis and Kediss are your commanders, your deck may contain cards with black and/or red in their color identity, but not cards with green, white, or blue.","oracle_id":"584cee10-f18c-4633-95cc-f2e7a11841ac","published_at":"2020-11-10","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Once the game begins, your two commanders are tracked separately. If you cast one, you won't have to pay an additional {2} the first time you cast the other. A player loses the game after having been dealt 21 damage from any one of them, not from both of them combined.","oracle_id":"584cee10-f18c-4633-95cc-f2e7a11841ac","published_at":"2020-11-10","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"To have two commanders, both must have the partner ability as the game begins. Losing the ability during the game doesn't cause either to cease to be your commander.","oracle_id":"584cee10-f18c-4633-95cc-f2e7a11841ac","published_at":"2020-11-10","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"You can choose two commanders with partner that are the same color or colors. In Commander Draft, you can even choose two of the same commander with partner if you drafted them. If you do this, make sure you keep the number of times you've cast each from the command zone clear for \"commander tax\" purposes.","oracle_id":"584cee10-f18c-4633-95cc-f2e7a11841ac","published_at":"2020-11-10","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If you put a creature card with bestow onto the battlefield, it will be a creature on the battlefield, not an Aura.","oracle_id":"b6f52260-9ad5-4024-acf9-d77f3c08c872","published_at":"2013-09-15","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If you put a creature card with {X} in its mana cost onto the battlefield, the value of that X is 0.","oracle_id":"b6f52260-9ad5-4024-acf9-d77f3c08c872","published_at":"2013-09-15","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Ashiok's second ability refers to any creature card exiled because of Ashiok's first or third ability.","oracle_id":"b6f52260-9ad5-4024-acf9-d77f3c08c872","published_at":"2013-09-15","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If Ashiok leaves the battlefield, and later another Ashiok enters the battlefield, it is a new object (even if the two were represented by the same card). Creature cards exiled by the original Ashiok can't be put onto the battlefield by the second ability of the new Ashiok.","oracle_id":"b6f52260-9ad5-4024-acf9-d77f3c08c872","published_at":"2013-09-15","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Ashiok's second ability doesn't target any creature card. You choose which creature card to return when that ability resolves, but you must choose one with mana value equal to the value you chose for X when activating the ability.","oracle_id":"b6f52260-9ad5-4024-acf9-d77f3c08c872","published_at":"2013-09-15","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If you somehow control a Kindred Discovery with no chosen creature type, its last ability can't trigger, even if a creature with no creature types enters the battlefield or attacks.","oracle_id":"005ee549-1bf5-478f-bc3f-3e791bd7eecf","published_at":"2017-08-25","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The choice of creature type is made as Kindred Discovery enters the battlefield. Players can't take any actions between the time the choice is made and the time it enters the battlefield. Notably, this means that if it is entering the battlefield at the same time as any creatures of the chosen type, its last ability will trigger.","oracle_id":"005ee549-1bf5-478f-bc3f-3e791bd7eecf","published_at":"2022-06-10","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"You must choose an existing creature type, such as Human or Warrior. Card types such as artifact and supertypes such as legendary can't be chosen.","oracle_id":"005ee549-1bf5-478f-bc3f-3e791bd7eecf","published_at":"2022-06-10","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"You can't choose multiple creature types, such as \"Cat Warrior.\" A Cat Warrior is both a Cat and a Warrior. It's affected by anything that affects either type and unaffected by things that affect non-Cat or non-Warrior creatures.","oracle_id":"005ee549-1bf5-478f-bc3f-3e791bd7eecf","published_at":"2023-09-01","source":"wotc"}],"schema_version":1,"source":"Pinned Scryfall originals for Ashiok's linked loyalty effects"}
